{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1482112-having-children-before-becoming-garou","id":1482112,"title":"Having children before becoming Garou","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-05-27T17:58:07-07:00","id":1482112,"title":"Having children before becoming Garou","content":"Hello<br /> If I remember correctly, Garou normally have their first change when they're teenagers. What if two garou have a child before going through the first change (teenage pregnancy and stuff)? Would that child be a Metis?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5394-argonot","name":"Argonot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-27T18:29:15-07:00","id":1482114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Argonot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1482112-having-children-before-becoming-garou#post1482112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello<br /> If I remember correctly, Garou normally have their first change when they're teenagers. What if two garou have a child before going through the first change (teenage pregnancy and stuff)? Would that child be a Metis?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would expect it to, the fact they didn't have the first change doesn't somehow make them &quot;not garou&quot;.<br /> In fact resources the Garou have to keep tabs on their cubs like kin fetch would go from occasionally unreliable to utterly useless if not outright impossible, were it so.<br /> <br /> Cubs or not, these youths are Garou already, they simply don't know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 05-27-2022, 09:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-27T19:37:14-07:00","id":1482118,"title":"","content":"To side-step the more creepy side of the subject, first change can also occur later in life before 25 years of age. Granted this is rare, so most garou could write-off a cub as a &quot;false alarm&quot; if they make it to their 20's without changing.<br /> <br /> So it's entirely plausible for two 22 year old &quot;false alarms&quot; to get married(possibly even with the local sects blessing if they're &quot;in the know&quot;) only to later have a first change.<br /> <br /> I imagine this would be like the garou equivalent of both parties finding out after marriage that they were actually direct siblings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-27T20:05:04-07:00","id":1482123,"title":"","content":"There have also been Garou who don't change until much later than 25 years old. It's just relatively rare. Some of those change &quot;normally&quot; - just later. And others could be Lunatics who suppressed the wolf inside them until something helped cause them to change.<br /> <br /> As for the child itself, yes it would be a metis. <br /> <br /> What kind of form that child is born in is something I would leave to the ST. Assuming the parents are both homid, I'd probably rule that despite being of the Metis breed the child itself would appear in the form of a Homid. But the Metis deformity (whatever it would be) would obviously still be present. However, I might depict the child in Crinos form for story purposes if I wanted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-27T23:20:48-07:00","id":1482129,"title":"","content":"Given how the books have traditionally described the requirements of a Garou-born pregnancy, either the mother would have to have her First Change near the start of the third trimester, or she'd die. The simplest solution would just for such a pregnancy to almost always result in a First Change for the mother baring some lore around the occasional tragedy when that doesn't happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-27T23:31:34-07:00","id":1482130,"title":"","content":"W20 has this line: Most werewolves go through their First Change at puberty, <b>but an increasing number don\u2019t hit until adulthood</b>. Homids can experience the First Change at any point between the ages of 14 and 21.<br /> <br /> And some other places that seem to retcon the revised edition stance that garou are born garou (and identifiable as such).<br /> <br /> It could very well be, that W20 authors intend that garou pre-change are not considered garou in many setting relevant circumstances and therefore any intercourse with one or both partners being pre-change would not result in a crinos-born child.<br /> <br /> Revised Edition was very clear about garou always being garou in and FAQ section. Therefore all the thoughts above apply.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-27T23:51:53-07:00","id":1482132,"title":"","content":"W20 removed auto-detecting them with a fairly common Rank 1 Gift. It still has ways of detecting them for characters invested in such. I think there's a lot more evidence that the W20 authors wanted to make finding pre-change Garou harder than it was in Revised, rather than changing their metaphysical status in other regards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-28T00:43:04-07:00","id":1482136,"title":"","content":"In first &quot;When will you rage&quot; one character says something like that:<br /> &quot;First Change doesn't make us Garou. It's The moment when we realise we are one.&quot;<br /> So I believe that yes, intercourse between 2 pre-change Garou would give a metis. But first I read once somewhere that most pregnancies like that end prematurely. And second I believe that, it humans intinctively sense something wrong about Garou even if they cannot name it, pre-change Garou can also sense another one. It's like with a girl/boy who turns up most of your friends but you cannot find anything attractive in her/him. So basically if you want intercourse between pre-change Garou they have to be stoned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-28T01:47:34-07:00","id":1482138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1482112-having-children-before-becoming-garou?p=1482132#post1482132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">W20 removed auto-detecting them with a fairly common Rank 1 Gift. It still has ways of detecting them for characters invested in such. I think there's a lot more evidence that the W20 authors wanted to make finding pre-change Garou harder than it was in Revised, rather than changing their metaphysical status in other regards.</div> </div> </div> </div>We had this discussion a couple of times and since there is no clear intent stated (that I know of), it is hard to know what the authors wanted.<br /> Was &quot;Baptism of Fire&quot; still stating &quot;Scent of the true form&quot; can discern pre-change garou an oversight or did one contributier to the book not know what changes the head writer intended?<br /> Was the &quot;Test Vial&quot; Talen being able to discern pre-change garou simply copy&amp;paste or is it intentionally the (as far as I see) only way in the rules to discern pre-change garou?<br /> If it was, why would W20:Kinfolk go on to talk about that every Kinfolk could have a first change basically at any moment.<br /> <br /> You might be right, that their only intent was to make their detection harder, but the way they did it leaves some questions unanswered....<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-28T13:39:36-07:00","id":1482192,"title":"","content":"Sure, if there was a clear answer here, it wouldn't get debated so frequently.<br /> <br /> I think we both agree that the W20 designers wanted there to be more uncertainty around detection. That's obvious in plenty of the text, not just things like Scent of the True Form being changed. But they didn't remove detection completely, nor did they remove things that rely on a successful detection (or at least a presumed to be one).<br /> <br /> The idea that Test Vials are &quot;the only way,&quot; flies in the face of the all of the Gift, Rite, Fetish, and Talen lists explicitly being examples/common powers, not exhaustive lists. If a Talen can do something, there's no reason presented in the books why there can't be a Fetish or Rite that can't do something similar enough. There's no reason why there can't be a Gift that can't.<br /> <br /> What we have, from the stuff that's in the books rather than conjecture about intent, is that the Garou have to actively check on an individual basis. You can't just have a Cliath Philodox walk down the street and automatically notice every pre-Change Garou, so their Sept can then rather easily gather up Lost Cubs. You have to have a reason to use a Test Vial, which is only good on one person before you have to make another, which makes it OK for the known children of Garou and kin deeply involved with them, but leaves lots of more peripheral kin and callow kin completely unable to access things like Test Vials to know if their kids are Garou or not.<br /> <br /> That's the big change that was made indisputably.<br /> <br /> But at long as detection is possible, then pre-Change Garou are not the same as kinfolk on a metaphysical level. In game characters might not be able to tell the difference until something happens, but out of character we can know things like two pre-Change teens having sex can result in a messy situation.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-28T14:16:41-07:00","id":1482196,"title":"","content":"But did really a Philodox walk down a street and sniff around? I mean it is a conscious act to activate the Gift, is it not? If it is not, what does that mean for Mokol\u00e9's &quot;Sight of true form&quot;?<br /> <br /> W20 made the roll against difficulty six and successes to determine..... what exactly?<br /> No success does not tell the garou anything, so the user knows it was a failure and re-rolls, right?<br /> One success tells the user it's a human or animal - but if it is a changeling (kithain, not inanimae or something like that) it is also a human, same goes for a ghoul or a mage. Does one success reveal &quot;human&quot; or does it reveal &quot;not human, not animal, not failure on the roll&quot;. If so - one success is a supernatural being detector.<br /> Also, Kinfolk is determined automatically. Doesn't specify if this is limited to garou kinfolk.<br /> <br /> The Gift was, imo, badly designed in revised and W20 did make it a bit better, but not much.<br /> On the other hand, now the difficulty is always 6, so botching became less likely. No more accidentally identifying the sorcerer as vampire.<br /> <br /> It should have been: ST rolls secretly, if there is not sufficient successes the person/animal smells the way he/she appears. Doesn't matter if one uses a difficulty or success threshold for the different critters. With the rule to make trivial tasks automatic successes the ST can still decide to tell the players if they smell garou (or kin) if one wants the automatic part of the Gift. Still, 'pre-change garou require always a roll' would have been an easy addition.<br /> <br /> ----<br /> <br /> But the subtext of W20 Kinfolk, at least the passages I read, goes very much into &quot;any kinfolk could have a first change anytime&quot; and that doesn't make sense, if there are means to test them and they are relatively easy to get by. Like you said, any tribe should have a Test Vial equivalent, possibly even a Fetish.<br /> <br /> I feel this whole affair is messy and was not discussed thoroughly before it was written into the book. A shift reducing the archetype &quot;pre-indoctrinated cubs raised by kenning kinfolk&quot; towards &quot;lost cubs&quot; way in my imagination the reason for this whole affair, and I don't like this either. I find pre-indoctrinated mono-tribal cliaths being confronted with multi-tribal and modern western human culture far more interesting than the average human being confronted with the garou tribal world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1008,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","user":"heinrich","date":". 05-28-2022, 05:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-28T21:41:43-07:00","id":1482216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1482112-having-children-before-becoming-garou?p=1482196#post1482196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But did really a Philodox walk down a street and sniff around? I mean it is a conscious act to activate the Gift, is it not?</div> </div> </div> </div>The wording in Revised is, &quot;The Garou can tell automatically when someone is a werewolf; anything else requires a Perception + Primal-Urge roll.&quot; And the Revised FAQ confirmed this applied to pre-Change Garou. There's only a need to activate it for other things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If it is not, what does that mean for Mokol\u00e9's &quot;Sight of true form&quot;? </div> </div> </div>Probably that they're meant to notice each other automatically, not Garou, but that's not what a strict reading of the rules would very imply in a very silly way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> W20 made the roll against difficulty six and successes to determine..... what exactly? </div> </div> </div>What someone is if they're not automatically detected as a Garou or kin.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No success does not tell the garou anything, so the user knows it was a failure and re-rolls, right? </div> </div> </div>The book doesn't specify. I would assume a failure would be recognized as such and a retry would be possible, but not rolling enough successes for the target true's supernatural nature would have the Garou conclude they're a normal human/animal/etc. One success on a mage would ping &quot;human,&quot; and the PC would need cause to roll again. This remains useful if you consider that means they could at least tell a vampire in the form of a wolf isn't actually a normal wolf (even if they don't know what it really is) as &quot;wolf&quot; isn't their natural state.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But the subtext of W20 Kinfolk,... </div> </div> </div>I think it's important to judge either Kinfolk book by the fact that both say that they're written from the perspective of playable kinfolk, not necessarily from the perspective of how WtA works as a whole. That is, to kinfolk, any other kin could First Change at any moment because they have no way of knowing for themselves who's kin and who's a pre-Change since Scent of the True Form pings them as the same. There are far more kin than Garou, not everyone is going to get tested, not every test is going to work correctly, etc. There's always a chance someone they think of as kin is really a Garou on the verge of popping without any warning. That's there to tell you what it's like to live as a kin, not necessarily to comment on the metaphysics of the setting.<br /> <br /> Trying to be respectful of recent US news...<br /> <br /> The vast majority of students in the USA will never experience someone coming into their school and shooting people. For as horrific as the rate of it happening here is, it's still someone most people will never directly experience. However, the rate at which it happens, and the danger of it happening anywhere, has also left deep traumatic scars in multiple generations of younger US citizens. I'm too old, you're from a country without this (and maybe too old, I don't know how old you are and it's not really important to my point), so it's hard to put yourself in their shoes. But for younger US citizens they have never known a life without a childhood of constantly worrying that today is the day when their school gets shot up. That constant anxiety and stress has measurable psychological effects.<br /> <br /> Kinfolk have been dealing with that for thousands of years. Even if most kinfolk will never experience a person they thought was kin but was actually pre-Change, and the damage that can cause, they've lived their whole life constantly worrying that today might be the day they're the unlucky one(s) that get clawed and mauled before anyone can help. That's burned into the minds of kinfolk over generations of no way to avoid that some number of kinfolk are going to suffer like that.<br /> <br /> To me, that's what Unsung Heroes and A Breed Apart are really trying to get at. What it's like to be powerless and uncertain in the fact of potential sudden violent and brutal death. The subtext is about understanding that psychology, not about Test Vials and Scent of the True Form.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I feel this whole affair is messy and was not discussed thoroughly before it was written into the book. </div> </div> </div><br /> Possibly, but my whole point was that we have books, we have what they say. We can figure out the most reasonable way to interpret them as they are without trying to speculate on the authors and their process. Once we acknowledge how things are, we can either accept them, or change them, as our individual games would benefit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-29T00:18:25-07:00","id":1482224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1482112-having-children-before-becoming-garou?p=1482216#post1482216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The wording in Revised is, &quot;The Garou can tell automatically when someone is a werewolf; anything else requires a Perception + Primal-Urge roll.&quot; And the Revised FAQ confirmed this applied to pre-Change Garou. There's only a need to activate it for other things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, I never read this as &quot;the Gift automatically activates when a person is a werewolf&quot;. I mean the Gift goes on about that actual smell is a requirement and that surrounding smells may hinder it.<br /> Even &quot;On Patrol&quot; only allows to automatically cast the Gift on a wyrm-tainted person....<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1482112-having-children-before-becoming-garou?p=1482216#post1482216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably that they're meant to notice each other automatically, not Garou, but that's not what a strict reading of the rules would very imply in a very silly way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Possibly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1482112-having-children-before-becoming-garou?p=1482216#post1482216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The book doesn't specify. I would assume a failure would be recognized as such and a retry would be possible, but not rolling enough successes for the target true's supernatural nature would have the Garou conclude they're a normal human/animal/etc. One success on a mage would ping &quot;human,&quot; and the PC would need cause to roll again. This remains useful if you consider that means they could at least tell a vampire in the form of a wolf isn't actually a normal wolf (even if they don't know what it really is) as &quot;wolf&quot; isn't their natural state.</div> </div> </div> </div>Before W20 I would have assumed that a supernatural person/animal registers as what it appears, when no successes were rolled. Now, 1 success is needed to register a human/animal. If the being you want to identify is requiring more successes and the ST pings it back as human, it would be kinda dishonest, for the PC had enough successes to identify human/animal correctly - giving a false positive on human/animal betrays the one (or two) successes rolled, I feel.<br /> <br /> Also, isn't Protean actual transformation, much like the Birthright of a Pooka? What about Sorcerers and Mages and Life contra Mind or Forces to appear as something else?<br /> And the Mokol\u00e9, would it register the wolf that is actually a garou only if the garou was homid- or crinos-born, since wolf is the actual form of a lupus-born garou?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1482112-having-children-before-becoming-garou?p=1482216#post1482216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's important to judge either Kinfolk book by the fact that both say that they're written from the perspective of playable kinfolk, not necessarily from the perspective of how WtA works as a whole. That is, to kinfolk, any other kin could First Change at any moment because they have no way of knowing for themselves who's kin and who's a pre-Change since Scent of the True Form pings them as the same. There are far more kin than Garou, not everyone is going to get tested, not every test is going to work correctly, etc. There's always a chance someone they think of as kin is really a Garou on the verge of popping without any warning. That's there to tell you what it's like to live as a kin, not necessarily to comment on the metaphysics of the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't the Test Vial a kinfolk talen? If a garou is identified or not, wouldn't that make the rounds in the community. I mean the garou parent, if one is present, would surely boast about a true born child more than about a kinfolk baby, so the community usually knows.<br /> Sure, there are exceptions and people who keep a secret about their children, like the Margrave, but I find the premise that the POV in the books doesn't know who is garou faulty.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1482112-having-children-before-becoming-garou?p=1482216#post1482216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kinfolk have been dealing with that for thousands of years. Even if most kinfolk will never experience a person they thought was kin but was actually pre-Change, and the damage that can cause, they've lived their whole life constantly worrying that today might be the day they're the unlucky one(s) that get clawed and mauled before anyone can help. That's burned into the minds of kinfolk over generations of no way to avoid that some number of kinfolk are going to suffer like that.<br /> <br /> To me, that's what Unsung Heroes and A Breed Apart are really trying to get at. What it's like to be powerless and uncertain in the fact of potential sudden violent and brutal death. The subtext is about understanding that psychology, not about Test Vials and Scent of the True Form.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never saw this context in the books.<br /> Unsung Heros had the older sister who was full of awe for the beauty of her brother's Crinos form, despite just having been in a traumatic car accident, iirc. Most of the book was framed by a scientist, who handled most stuff scientifically, iirc. But 2nd Edition would have allowed to easily discern pre-change garou in the kenning kilfolk community and possibly even one or two layers of family relations away from the closes associates. So, this problem was mainly something that kinfolk disassociated with the garou had, but they didn't necessarily live in fear, for they didn't know about the danger.<br /> <br /> W20's approach is different there, and I can see that this fear is something that might be inherit in their lives now, more than it was before.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1482112-having-children-before-becoming-garou?p=1482216#post1482216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Possibly, but my whole point was that we have books, we have what they say. We can figure out the most reasonable way to interpret them as they are without trying to speculate on the authors and their process. Once we acknowledge how things are, we can either accept them, or change them, as our individual games would benefit.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. To me it always interesting to see who other players/STs see the world differently, simply be taking something different away from the written text","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-29T04:48:17-07:00","id":1482240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Argonot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1482112-having-children-before-becoming-garou#post1482112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello<br /> If I remember correctly, Garou normally have their first change when they're teenagers. What if two garou have a child before going through the first change (teenage pregnancy and stuff)? Would that child be a Metis?</div> </div> </div> </div>The child is aways a metis. It doesn't matter if you don't know it, you are a Garou from birth.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Werewolf, The Apocalypse - Storytellers Handbook, Revised, pg.20</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Are werewolves considered Kinfolk before the First Change?</b><br /> No, they are not. They\u2019re werewolves from the moment of birth. For instance, if they have kids with another Garou before undergoing the First Change, the progeny will be metis.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1482112-having-children-before-becoming-garou?p=1482123#post1482123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What kind of form that child is born in is something I would leave to the ST. Assuming the parents are both homid, I'd probably rule that despite being of the Metis breed the child itself would appear in the form of a Homid. But the Metis deformity (whatever it would be) would obviously still be present. However, I might depict the child in Crinos form for story purposes if I wanted.</div> </div> </div> </div>The child is aways born in Crinos. The books are very explicit about this. And the mother who hasn't gone through the First Change always dies in childbirth.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Werewolf, The Apocalypse - Players Guide to Garou, Revised, pg.57</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Could two unknowing homids breed and have a metis child before their First Change?</b><br /> <br /> Yes, technically, it\u2019s possible. Many homids have viable parts, as it were, at the beginning of puberty. Most of the time, their First Change will occur about the same time, and they\u2019ll be dragged willy-nilly into werewolf society around that point. So chances are good they\u2019ll know they shouldn\u2019t be mating before they actually can mate. (Lost cubs, of course, are the exception.) Moreover, unless the female undergoes First Change before the baby is born, she\u2019ll die, not being able to shift into Crinos. And finally, consider that the chances for a miscarriage are higher; a barely pubescent body is going to have a difficult time carrying any child to term, much less a metis. All in all, it\u2019s a highly improbable scenario.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13644,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13644-ghostwalker","user":"Ghostwalker","date":". 05-29-2022, 08:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13644-ghostwalker","name":"Ghostwalker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-29T14:11:34-07:00","id":1482288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1482112-having-children-before-becoming-garou?p=1482224#post1482224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't the Test Vial a kinfolk talen? If a garou is identified or not, wouldn't that make the rounds in the community. I mean the garou parent, if one is present, would surely boast about a true born child more than about a kinfolk baby, so the community usually knows.<br /> Sure, there are exceptions and people who keep a secret about their children, like the Margrave, but I find the premise that the POV in the books doesn't know who is garou faulty.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're ignoring the logistics of it.<br /> <br /> The thing is, even among Kinfolk in-the-know, an actual Werewolf still has just a 10% chance of having a Garou child with a Kinfolk. IIRC Two Kinfolk together has something between 1% and 0.1% chance. And all things considered, you can expect that most children in a Kinfolk community are the child of two Kinfolk.<br /> <br /> It means that in the best scenario the children of a perfectly Garou-friendly community will be Kinfolk 98.89% of the time, about eleven in each one thousand children are Garou. In the worst case a community should expect a Garou only once per thousand births.<br /> <br /> Now lets reverse the perspective. Where do Talens come from? Fetish-making Kinfolk are rare, most Talens are coming from Garou, and from specialized Garou on top of that. They have a lot of other concerns, and can't dedicate themselves solely to produce this one Talen. While far easier to produce in bulk than Fetishes, Talens are still handmade by what amounts to some of the rarer and most specialized craftsmen in the world, that are <i>not</i> dedicated to make Test Vials exclusively, or even particularly.<br /> <br /> Which proportion of Garou actually create Test Vials? How much time they dedicate to it, that is, how many Test Vials do they really create? How many Kinfolk children are out there to be tested? With this numbers alone we can expect at least 100 Kinfolk for each Garou, out there and having children. If you run the numbers for a time and account for the far lower life expectancy of Garou due to violence (most won't dedicate a lot of time to have children nor live much beyond 30 yo), probably the number of Kinfolk even in a in-the-know community is far greater than that.<br /> <br /> Getting Test Vials for every single birth means producing large quantities of it and delivering to every community, then an extra to compensate for Vials lost or destroyed in the way, because you can't expect perfect deliveries all the time at such a scale. And then you just have the risk of the Vial failing for whatever reason, like not being administered correctly. What's the cost of it in terms not only of money, but other valuable resources and time and attention of Garou that need to also focus on other things? What when anything disrupts the supply chain? You ask Kinfolk to stop having babies?<br /> <br /> All things considered, the most likely scenario is simply that most Kinfolk children won't ever be tested. They'll get the Vials they have and decide how to use it to maximize efficacy as they can, but with a resource that is essentially scarce for the task at hand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-30T02:48:14-07:00","id":1482355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghostwalker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1482112-having-children-before-becoming-garou?p=1482240#post1482240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The child is aways born in Crinos. The books are very explicit about this. And the mother who hasn't gone through the First Change always dies in childbirth.</div> </div> </div> </div>That may be so, but I think it's fine for the ST to change official rulings when needed. First edition material often had metis babies spontaneously change to a different form so there is precedent. The metis NPC Fengy mentioned in first and second edition corebooks was thrown into a reservoir at birth, and leaped out in lupus form which he spent for the rest of his life until the First Change. The metis NPC Hacktalon mentioned in Valkenburg Foundation was raise in a Catholic orphanage which implies he must have somehow been in homid form before his First Change.<br /> <br /> Normally I would always have metis born in crinos form, but certain unusual situations might lend themselves to an interesting story, and STs should be empowered to make exceptions if it provides an interesting scenario for the PCs. In this case, having the pre-changed Garou be parents, but still not understand what they and their child are, could be a good scene.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-30T03:14:47-07:00","id":1482359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1482112-having-children-before-becoming-garou?p=1482355#post1482355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That may be so, but I think it's fine for the ST to change official rulings when needed. First edition material often had metis babies spontaneously change to a different form so there is precedent. The metis NPC Fengy mentioned in first and second edition corebooks was thrown into a reservoir at birth, and leaped out in lupus form which he spent for the rest of his life until the First Change. The metis NPC Hacktalon mentioned in Valkenburg Foundation was raise in a Catholic orphanage which implies he must have somehow been in homid form before his First Change.<br /> <br /> Normally I would always have metis born in crinos form, but certain unusual situations might lend themselves to an interesting story, and STs should be empowered to make exceptions if it provides an interesting scenario for the PCs. In this case, having the pre-changed Garou be parents, but still not understand what they and their child are, could be a good scene.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course, storyteller got the right to change anything, even, if he desires, allow the PCs to slay the Wyrm itself (I knew a guy who could try that). But, as far as I remember, metis birth form is always crinos. Of course, there was also said that metis change forms more easily (but without any bonus for transformation rolls). Even your first example, Fengy, was born in crinos, assuming lupus form after he was thrown out. So in my opinion it would not be possible for metis to be born in homid (using logic of course) but if he is some Gaia's chosen one. <br /> <br /> And I believe that a pair of pre-change homids looking at USG and seeing their child with a wolf's head could be better for roleplaying. Especially if the mother is a PC, more so if she is an adult garou. Not to mention the doctor's face.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-30T16:23:02-07:00","id":1482417,"title":"","content":"The change to Homid could be a survival reaction similar to changing into Lupus to swim out of the reservoir, but in the uterus. Even inside the uterus fetuses start early to show movement and some elaborate reactions. They're not really developed, but are still acting for their own survival and learning far earlier than some people think.<br /> <br /> Given that the Homid uterus isn't an adequate place for a Metis fetus, the baby changing in reaction to the mother <i>not</i> changing could be a survival reflex kicking in. Since it isn't meant to be this early, it wouldn't be reliable by any measure, and many a still-born Metis could have died from a mishap in such an early change or changing to an inappropriate form that can't survive in a human uterus. The number of successful changes would be low enough that for an already rare occurrence (two pre-changers having a baby) the result would be as rare as to be unheard of.<br /> <br /> Of course, there's also the possibility of the mother undergoing the Change, either First Changing during pregnancy or going through this weird &quot;pre-Change-Change&quot; where her body goes into Crinos, or just Glabro, to survive the pregnancy, but doesn't really develop full Werewolf properties yet.<br /> <br /> Another possibility not discussed and maybe more likely would be a pre-Change mating with a developed Garou. The partner being actually a pre-Change isn't something the Garou will pick up immediately, and if no one suspects this &quot;Kinfolk&quot; to be Garou, a union after they grow up wouldn't be unthinkable. Teenage hormones can also play a factor in a Werewolf getting along with a Kinfolk without ever waiting to be sure, because the risk is low and they're horny as all Hell. That could, depending on circumstances, lead to an even bigger shock.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-30T22:35:47-07:00","id":1482462,"title":"","content":"Hello,<br /> <br /> Check the Guardians of the Caerns Metamorph Merit descriprion.<br /> That Merit let's the metis to change even in uterus. That's the exception from the Chrinos-born rule.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","name":"Lachdanan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T07:06:10-07:00","id":1482601,"title":"","content":"In terms of metis switching to other forms in utero/birth, I personally feel it should be extremely rare or very common. Especially as there is no metis birth that is not traumatic, so what triggers the merit is very much up to the air.<br /> <br /> It being either extremely rare or common and those who can't are the outliers preserves the issue of where the metis grows up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}